menu "Bluetooth"

config BT_LE
    bool "Bluetooth Low Energy (central)"
    default y
    depends on RADIO_CYW43
    help
      Scanning, connecting, GATT discovery, read/write/subscribe and SMP
      bonding, via BTstack's gatt_client. This is the transport the project
      leads with. On the Pico the controller is the CYW43439 (RADIO_CYW43).

config BT_CLASSIC
    bool "Bluetooth Classic (RFCOMM)"
    default n
    depends on BT_LE
    help
      Inquiry, SDP, and one RFCOMM session per link. A PEX module or a
      websocket op supplies the service UUID, the security policy, and any
      PIN. LE central stays available. MAX_NR_HCI_CONNECTIONS is shared,
      so turning this on costs ACL buffer RAM. The ACL payload is
      BT_ACL_PAYLOAD. Off in the default image. BNEP is BT_CLASSIC_NAP.

config BT_ACL_PAYLOAD
    int "Classic ACL payload bytes"
    depends on BT_CLASSIC
    default 1695 if BT_CLASSIC_NAP
    default 1021
    range 259 1695
    help
      HCI ACL payload, including the 4-byte L2CAP header. 1021 offers an
      RFCOMM MTU of 1017. 1695 is what BNEP needs so the Configure Request
      can offer MTU 1691. The NAP image keeps 1695.

config BT_CLASSIC_NAP
    bool "Bluetooth Classic BNEP / NAP uplink"
    default n
    depends on BT_CLASSIC
    depends on NET_UPLINK
    help
      A PANU connection to a phone NAP, and a NAP the phone can call.
      The netif ("b0") joins the uplink choice with Wi-Fi, Ethernet and
      USB-NCM when the phone is sharing its network. Off unless this
      option is on.

config BT_PERIPHERAL
    bool "BLE peripheral beside the central"
    default n
    depends on BT_LE
    help
      Advertise a connectable peripheral while the central keeps scanning.
      Lua and a PEX module can replace the local service list at runtime.
      One of those services can be MCUmgr SMP, so an image can arrive over
      BLE as well as UDP 1337. Off in the default image, and the central
      path is unchanged while it is off.

config BT_MAX_LINKS
    int "Concurrent links (all transports)"
    default 4
    range 1 8
    help
      Sized so a Lua profile can hold a device while a browser independently
      pokes another. Each link costs roughly 1 KB of GATT database plus
      BTstack's own per-connection state.

config GATT_MAX_SVCS
    int "Max services cached per device"
    default 16

config GATT_MAX_CHRS
    int "Max characteristics cached per device"
    default 160
    help
      Real devices have far more than a handful. A Pinecil V2 exposes over a
      hundred across its live-data, bulk and settings services, and a cap below
      that silently returns a partial tree.

config GATT_MAX_DSCS
    int "Max descriptors cached per device"
    default 48

config GATT_MAX_UUID128
    int "Max distinct 128-bit UUIDs interned per device"
    default 96
    help
      BTstack hands us a full uuid128 in every service, characteristic and
      descriptor. Interning them per device is what keeps a typical peripheral
      at about 1 KB instead of several.

endmenu
